// ==================== DISPLAY OUTPUT ====================
// Three layers, not two:
//
//   drawInner()      composes the frame into PSRAM. This is the DISPLAY LOGIC.
//                    It does not know or care where the pixels end up.
//   presentInner()   gets that frame onto whatever output exists, and owns the
//                    rate limit. On the finished PCB this becomes the SPI push
//                    to the panel; the streamer becomes optional.
//   sendScreenDiff() the streamer. Development only - there is no bridge on the
//                    real phone.
//
// renderInner() is still drawInner() + presentInner(), so all 103 existing call
// sites are untouched.
//
// Why throttling the stream is safe: sendScreenDiff() diffs against `last`,
// which is what the BRIDGE HAS ACTUALLY RECEIVED - not the previous frame. So a
// skipped send loses nothing, and the next one carries everything that piled up
// meanwhile. A skipped frame just sets inDirty, and the 60ms retry loop already
// in loop() collects it.
//
// A max RATE, not a divisor: a divisor depends on how often render happens, and
// that swings from once a second for the clock to 30/sec for a game.
//
// 30 here effectively means "do not throttle" - a full inner frame is 4.5 MB/s
// at 30fps and the link already refuses strips at 3. Lower it to watch the OS
